+# REVIEW: duration-store
+
+## 🎯 Round 1 Summary
+Grade **A** (P0 0, P1 0, P2 4, P3 9). All 7 lenses exercised. Single full-context pass: the files are new, so Pass 1 redaction was skipped. Nothing was auto-fixed, because the grade met the threshold. Confirmation pass `confirm-1` returned no findings from any lens.
+
+## 🔍 Drift Findings
+None. Changed files: `timeparse/store.py`, `tests/test_store.py`, plus the SPEC, PLAN and REVIEW documents. All five SPEC scenarios have tests.
+
+## ✅ Consensus Findings
+No P0 or P1. All findings below are `consensus-passed` (solo-lens vote) at P2/P3, disposition `accepted`, and **carried unfixed**; they do not move the grade.
+
+P2:
+- `timeparse/store.py:40` (functionality): a newly created file keeps mkstemp mode 0600; only an existing target's mode is preserved (ADR-003 covers existing files only). Not documented or tested.
+- `timeparse/store.py:42` (security): `os.replace` swaps a symlinked target for a regular file, while the mode is read through the link. SPEC left symlink semantics open.
+- `timeparse/store.py:55` (security): deeply nested JSON raises `RecursionError`, which is not a `ValueError`, so a caller catching only `ValueError` is bypassed.
+- `tests/test_store.py:117` (consistency): the "write failure" test injects at `os.fdopen` (closed fd), so a failure after a partial `json.dump` is not exercised.
+
+P3: fd not closed if `os.fdopen` raises; cleanup `unlink` error can mask the original exception; `exists()`/`stat()` TOCTOU; temp-name prefix can exceed NAME_MAX for very long target names; `load_durations` accepts negative and huge ints; no `KeyboardInterrupt` cleanup test. A stale S4 test name in the SPEC table was fixed in place (documentation only).
